findings.problem:
This first-round major was not touched by the fix round, and the count has gone from 45 to 51 whole-value style holes. format.md allows a style hole only for live, state-driven values or a declared tweak prop, never for static theme tokens. Several holes are constant strings:
- c.line2Style (main.js:151);
- f.queueStyle (main.js:222), new in this round;
- L.ftlTopStyle (main.js:254).
rootStyle (main.js:270) carries the static background, colour and font. Every style on the Status key is static, and that artboard has no props at all. Holding these as holes keeps Tamsin from restyling the elements in the properties panel, which edits only literal inline styles, and the board paints unstyled while it streams in. Nothing breaks at runtime.

SKILL.md limits an imported file's helmet to a font <link>, an uploaded @font-face and body{margin:0}. Main's helmet still holds:
- a body background;
- the global button reset;
- the .uh-* hover and active rules;
- button:focus-visible;
- the scrollbar rules;
- the a/a:hover colours.
The runtime copies them into each importer today, so the five wrappers render correctly, but they depend on rules the format does not promise to carry.

Partly fixed: the segments, queue arrows, back button, radios, focus rows and era pill are now 44 px. Measured on the Phone artboard in the real runtime, though:
- the 250 breakthrough chips (buttons) are 36 px;
- the 135 run-label buttons are 36 px;
- the 5 section headers are 40 px;
- the 8 era-band headers are 24 px.
That contradicts the board title and the canvas rule that touch targets are at least 44 px.

rechecks.verdict:
From the canvas-format lens this is ready to show Tamsin. All seven artboards keep the rules that fail silently:
- the exact support.js head line;
- every element closed and every attribute quoted;
- holes that are dotted lookups or literals only;
- hint attributes on every sc-if and sc-for;
- whole-value event attributes;
- classic `class Component extends DCLogic` with no script-built DOM;
- valid data-props JSON;
- no emoji (★ ✓ ✗ are text dingbats in the font subset);
- inline SVG icons and real buttons;
- the font as a /_blob/ @font-face;
- dc-import never self-closed and no prop named name.

I checked this with a static linter and by running all seven in the canvas's own dc-runtime.js, which is byte-identical to the published one. Every artboard loads with zero console messages and the font loads. Main.dc.html matches what assemble.py builds from src/. The published project files are byte-for-byte the same size as the local ones.

Every new construct works in the real runtime:
- **componentDidUpdate re-init:** switching view or phone resets the scene.
- **Disabled holes:** there is no disabled attribute when the value is false, and the button is disabled when it is true.
- **Ref callback:** the phone focus list scrolls to 765 px, both in the wrapper and after toggling phone through the Tweak.
- **phone="{{ true }}":** the child receives a real boolean.
- **onContextMenu on both buttons:** right-click queues the focus and suppresses the native menu.

All first-review blockers are fixed, and so are all majors except one. The format major on static tokens in style holes was not addressed and has grown from 45 to 51 holes. It breaks nothing, but it keeps those styles out of the properties panel. Five minors remain:
- Main's over-full helmet;
- four live-looking buttons that do nothing;
- phone targets below the 44 px the board title promises;
- status copy that exists only in JS, with the status-4 wording in three variants;
- 12-px text reintroduced in the Endeavour pill.
